WEBVTT


00:00:47.388 --> 00:00:53.378
Early 21st century. Robot technology
undergoes massive development.


00:00:53.978 --> 00:00:56.718
By mid-century,
Japan leads the world


00:00:56.858 --> 00:01:00.098
in robot knowledge and application.


00:01:00.232 --> 00:01:03.228
From domestic uses to weaponry,


00:01:03.398 --> 00:01:05.522
Japan dominates the world market.


00:01:06.238 --> 00:01:09.318
As the technology is extended
to the human body


00:01:09.445 --> 00:01:11.650
the mood of
the international community


00:01:11.788 --> 00:01:14.154
turns againtst use of humanoids.


00:01:14.414 --> 00:01:17.990
Just as with nuclear power
and biotechnology before,


00:01:18.122 --> 00:01:21.739
U.N regulations are proposed


00:01:21.922 --> 00:01:24.117
to limit robot technology.


00:01:25.047 --> 00:01:29.088
Japan fiercely
resists this limitation


00:01:29.258 --> 00:01:32.124
but the will of the U.N.
is unshakeable.


00:01:32.851 --> 00:01:38.097
Japan takes the extreme step
of withdrawing from the U.N.


00:01:38.226 --> 00:01:40.428
And begins a new policy
of national isolation.


00:01:43.194 --> 00:01:47.229
Japan uses it high technology
to withdraw from world affairs.


00:01:47.361 --> 00:01:49.850
10 years go by.


00:01:50.494 --> 00:01:53.146
The resulting information blackout


00:01:53.281 --> 00:01:56.362
turns Japan into a total enigma.


00:01:59.455 --> 00:02:01.739
For an entire decade,


00:02:02.039 --> 00:02:06.747
no foreigner penetrates the veil.


00:02:43.128 --> 00:02:44.866
This is disrupting
my entire holiday.


00:02:45.502 --> 00:02:49.744
Now that your family has alredy
left Washington for Denver.


00:02:50.093 --> 00:02:51.832
Don't the Japanese


00:02:51.968 --> 00:02:54.215
understand it's Christmas?


00:02:54.679 --> 00:02:56.800
Dragging us miles out here...


00:02:58.304 --> 00:03:01.423
At least the British, French
and Russians are here, too.


00:04:47.621 --> 00:04:51.994
"S.W.O.R.D."


00:04:55.054 --> 00:04:57.163
The R.A.C.E.


00:05:01.303 --> 00:05:04.383
Final stand-by. We go in on my mark.


00:05:07.191 --> 00:05:09.516
Dumb gig. Dumb time of year.


00:05:10.355 --> 00:05:13.660
Just some Christmas party, right...


00:05:14.193 --> 00:05:15.768
Do the job quick


00:05:16.151 --> 00:05:17.981
and you'll home
for Mom's Turkey.


00:05:38.506 --> 00:05:43.551
Each of the wolrd's nations has
debated the issue of human evolution


00:05:44.140 --> 00:05:47.340
and come to
the exact same conclusion.


00:05:48.521 --> 00:05:51.637
Thus we can say that this result


00:05:52.352 --> 00:05:56.812
represents a true and just future
for humanity.


00:05:59.033 --> 00:06:04.693
If we at Daiwa Heavy Industries
have your endorsement,


00:06:05.244 --> 00:06:08.527
I'd appreciate a round of applause.


00:06:16.717 --> 00:06:18.164
Didn't think so...


00:06:44.658 --> 00:06:46.940
The primary target is Saito
of Daiwa Heavy Industries.


00:06:48.745 --> 00:06:51.652
We're working on a tip-off.
It might be a trap.


00:06:51.877 --> 00:06:55.206
Keep zour eyes open.


00:06:56.753 --> 00:07:01.079
I said we didn't need 'em.
Why so many rorbots?


00:07:01.341 --> 00:07:04.041
No idea. Ask the chief...


00:07:04.345 --> 00:07:06.587
They're the latest Daiwa models.


00:07:06.893 --> 00:07:08.877
Latest or not,


00:07:10.392 --> 00:07:12.214
I don't trust them.


00:09:32.329 --> 00:09:33.313
S.W.O.R.D.?


00:09:36.415 --> 00:09:37.698
Darn you, Maria...


00:10:24.961 --> 00:10:26.327
Get out of my way!


00:12:46.442 --> 00:12:47.558
Darn.


00:13:01.119 --> 00:13:02.863
Dispose of all the bodies.


00:13:17.222 --> 00:13:18.962
What the heck's going on?


00:13:19.097 --> 00:13:21.463
What's SWORD doing here?


00:13:21.850 --> 00:13:25.132
Answer me.
Don't you know who I am?


00:13:25.603 --> 00:13:28.968
For God's sake, I demand to know.


00:13:37.368 --> 00:13:38.225
Leon!


00:14:24.079 --> 00:14:30.031
"VEXILLE"


00:16:36.041 --> 00:16:39.031
"SWORD HQ, Los Angeles"


00:17:01.696 --> 00:17:04.516
It's a flagrant violation
of international treaties.


00:17:05.693 --> 00:17:07.475
Wich ones?


00:17:07.613 --> 00:17:10.651
They ingnored just about every one.


00:17:12.574 --> 00:17:14.568
Which part is metallic?


00:17:14.785 --> 00:17:17.278
Well, it's bio-metal.


00:17:17.706 --> 00:17:20.030
So this was his only robotic part?


00:17:21.673 --> 00:17:23.368
I hope that's the case.


00:17:23.714 --> 00:17:26.667
But during the raid
we confirmed his bio-signature.


00:17:26.926 --> 00:17:29.877
It might've been added later.


00:17:30.008 --> 00:17:31.883
Is that even possible?


00:17:32.890 --> 00:17:34.545
Not with our technology.


00:17:36.182 --> 00:17:40.842
If Japan is manufacturing
androids of this level...


00:17:40.979 --> 00:17:43.932
It would pose a threat
equal to nuclear power.


00:17:44.197 --> 00:17:48.025
This mean Saito's an android?


00:17:50.612 --> 00:17:53.068
In any case,


00:17:53.200 --> 00:17:55.859
there's nothing comparable
in the US, legit or otherwise.


00:17:56.371 --> 00:17:59.866
It'll take forever
to reverse-engineer.


00:18:00.749 --> 00:18:03.239
This reminds me of San Pedro
last month.


00:18:14.977 --> 00:18:16.049
Zak...


00:18:39.081 --> 00:18:42.280
Despite all the people
living in this city.


00:18:42.534 --> 00:18:48.665
We only talk to people with
this badge or to our darn computers.


00:18:49.384 --> 00:18:50.873
It's not the city's fault.


00:18:51.179 --> 00:18:52.672
It's the age we live in.


00:18:55.594 --> 00:18:56.920
Anything from Irene?


00:19:02.102 --> 00:19:03.595
Not a word.


00:19:04.271 --> 00:19:05.598
Sorry...


00:19:07.564 --> 00:19:11.814
Hear anything about San Pedro
from Leon?


00:19:15.245 --> 00:19:16.488
Really...


00:19:19.497 --> 00:19:22.284
Was the tip-off for this misson
from San Pedro?


00:19:22.416 --> 00:19:23.446
Correct.


00:19:23.958 --> 00:19:26.408
Not that it's a secret any more.


00:19:34.222 --> 00:19:38.701
"Port of San Pedro"


00:20:21.890 --> 00:20:24.966
Why the need for us to guard this?


00:20:25.142 --> 00:20:28.888
That's the latest
Japanese weapon system.


00:20:29.070 --> 00:20:31.722
But any enemy would have 'em, too.


00:20:31.864 --> 00:20:34.358
The battlefield is Japan's
showroom after all.


00:20:34.694 --> 00:20:39.731
It's not right that everyone
treats Japan special.


00:20:41.583 --> 00:20:43.524
Some day, they'll get
what they deserve.


00:21:27.584 --> 00:21:29.952
Cease pursuit and withdraw.


00:21:30.085 --> 00:21:31.660
You've got to be kidding.


00:21:32.380 --> 00:21:35.456
I repeat, caese pursuit immediately.


00:21:35.803 --> 00:21:37.870
This is our turf.


00:22:08.956 --> 00:22:10.029
Zak!


00:23:17.814 --> 00:23:19.059
Be careful.


00:23:20.861 --> 00:23:22.189
SWORD...


00:23:22.911 --> 00:23:26.982
December...23rd...Mt. Filar...


00:23:27.578 --> 00:23:29.987
Beware...of a meeting.


00:23:30.786 --> 00:23:32.236
Maria...


00:23:47.265 --> 00:23:51.508
Leon trusted
the fugitive completely.


00:23:54.118 --> 00:23:55.099
I mean,


00:23:55.229 --> 00:23:58.017
even now I can't belive
it was an android.


00:23:59.738 --> 00:24:01.021
Function-wise?


00:24:01.152 --> 00:24:03.937
You couldn't tell it wasn't human.


00:24:04.365 --> 00:24:05.814
Might it have been?


00:24:05.951 --> 00:24:08.695
There was
absolutely no bio-signature.


00:24:09.414 --> 00:24:10.985
But those eyes...


00:24:13.168 --> 00:24:14.536
Autospy results?


00:24:15.079 --> 00:24:16.575
They sent the android back to Japan


00:24:16.712 --> 00:24:19.531
after political pressure.


00:24:19.670 --> 00:24:20.910
In the end...


00:24:22.300 --> 00:24:25.789
they hardly laid a finger on it.


00:24:27.971 --> 00:24:29.384
Really...


00:24:34.684 --> 00:24:35.800
Maria...


00:24:36.561 --> 00:24:40.098
Japan. Completely off our screens
for an entire decade.


00:24:40.649 --> 00:24:43.651
But we ignore its


00:24:43.657 --> 00:24:46.021
recent suspicious
activity at our peril.


00:24:46.821 --> 00:24:48.486
We still don't know


00:24:48.656 --> 00:24:50.358
the purpose of
the meeting at Mt. Filar.


00:24:51.247 --> 00:24:56.199
But a State Dept. Order says
the politician we detained there


00:24:56.332 --> 00:24:59.247
must be returned to his duties.


00:25:00.461 --> 00:25:06.751
There's also strong pressure
from Japan to return Saito's limb.


00:25:09.893 --> 00:25:12.672
As for the results of the autospy,


00:25:12.849 --> 00:25:16.506
it's composed of
undetecable bio-metal.


00:25:17.016 --> 00:25:20.552
Judging from bio-signature analysis,


00:25:21.733 --> 00:25:26.145
we strongly suspect Saito is
an android.


00:25:28.904 --> 00:25:34.070
Android production is a grave
violation of international treaties.


00:25:37.294 --> 00:25:41.243
Nonetheless, the White House
is urging caution.


00:25:41.375 --> 00:25:43.741
Any action that


00:25:45.045 --> 00:25:51.173
might harm good relations
with Japan, is forbidden.


00:25:53.890 --> 00:25:57.638
But Japan is up to something.


00:26:00.480 --> 00:26:05.849
Henceforth we at SWORD
will be on our own.


00:26:06.363 --> 00:26:07.565
No matter what happens,


00:26:07.692 --> 00:26:10.149
you can forget about
goverment protection.


00:26:14.198 --> 00:26:18.993
We are to face this threat
to international society


00:26:19.670 --> 00:26:22.405
and neutralize it by our own means.


00:26:25.336 --> 00:26:27.119
Our mission this time:


00:26:29.718 --> 00:26:31.877
to infiltrate Fortress Japan.


00:26:33.763 --> 00:26:37.633
Japan has been veiled in mystery
for 10 yers.


00:26:37.806 --> 00:26:40.884
The time has come to unmask it.


00:26:51.534 --> 00:26:55.939
These images are of Tokyo
10 yers ago.


00:26:57.079 --> 00:27:01.199
As you know, no-one has been there
since its seclusion.


00:27:02.129 --> 00:27:04.321
Its most powerful corporation,
Daiwa Heavy Industries,


00:27:04.463 --> 00:27:07.036
has dominated the economy
for the past yers of isolation.


00:27:07.172 --> 00:27:10.333
Daiwa dictates Japan's politics
and controls all aspects of life.


00:27:11.302 --> 00:27:15.461
We also guess that it's behind
the policy of national isolation.


00:27:16.143 --> 00:27:19.381
Japan's high-tech seclusion
is made possible


00:27:19.514 --> 00:27:21.593
by an electro-magnetic network
named R.A.C.E.


00:27:22.476 --> 00:27:29.138
It relies on 270 sea-based antennas
covering the entire archipelago.


00:27:29.908 --> 00:27:35.103
As you know, it filters out
all waves and light reaching Japan


00:27:35.497 --> 00:27:38.524
and scrambles outbound signals


00:27:39.498 --> 00:27:43.031
to create a total barrie
to all transmissions


00:27:43.171 --> 00:27:45.828
rendering even satellite
surveillance worthless.


00:27:47.209 --> 00:27:50.877
Your mission is to penetrate
the electromagnetic field


00:27:51.056 --> 00:27:55.831
then transmit a reverse beacon
to unscramble the diffusion barrier.


00:27:56.675 --> 00:27:58.250
If successful,


00:27:58.386 --> 00:28:02.173
this will facilitate
direct satellite surveillance.


00:28:02.932 --> 00:28:06.188
The beacon transmission from Tokyo


00:28:06.317 --> 00:28:11.013
must last at least 3 minutes
for the satellite to align.


00:28:11.983 --> 00:28:14.354
One problem is your entry route.


00:28:14.731 --> 00:28:17.728
All waters and airspace


00:28:17.865 --> 00:28:21.778
are guarded by a warning system
on a technological par with R.A.C.E.


00:28:22.494 --> 00:28:26.828
Not even a micro-recon craft,
much less a person,


00:28:26.964 --> 00:28:28.248
can get through.


00:28:49.812 --> 00:28:53.849
After you send
the beacon transmission


00:28:54.109 --> 00:28:57.852
the infiltration team will press
further into Japan


00:28:58.079 --> 00:29:02.237
to gain as much information
as possible about Daiwa Industries.


00:29:02.589 --> 00:29:07.951
72 hours later you'll meet at a
predetermined extraction point.


00:29:27.268 --> 00:29:29.511
Commander Leon Fayden


00:29:29.693 --> 00:29:33.429
has volunteered
to lead this dangerous mission.


00:29:34.487 --> 00:29:37.862
10 years ago
he was dispatched to Japan


00:29:37.992 --> 00:29:41.987
leading an anti-terrorist task unit
helping Japanese security.


00:29:42.664 --> 00:29:45.236
They suddenly shut the borders


00:29:45.412 --> 00:29:48.487
but he was there
until forcefully repatriated.


00:29:59.256 --> 00:30:00.753
Why didn't you tell me?


00:30:02.263 --> 00:30:04.420
I didn't want you to worry.


00:30:04.555 --> 00:30:06.086
Not about volunteering...


00:30:06.264 --> 00:30:07.847
the fact that you were in Japan.


00:30:10.309 --> 00:30:12.393
I never had a chance to.


00:30:12.520 --> 00:30:14.101
Is that the only reason?


00:30:15.865 --> 00:30:17.315
Yes, it is.


00:30:32.672 --> 00:30:35.492
Didn't want you involved...


00:32:02.470 --> 00:32:04.291
Bring up the deck monitor!


00:32:06.351 --> 00:32:09.134
This vessel is not damaged
or under attack.


00:32:09.644 --> 00:32:12.928
A nearby US cargo ship
just exploded.


00:32:13.146 --> 00:32:14.800
We are investigating the cause.


00:32:14.976 --> 00:32:17.140
Just in case,
let's go to emergency status.


00:33:07.447 --> 00:33:09.987
Freight inspections all complete.


00:33:23.381 --> 00:33:24.812
Safely past border security.


00:33:25.012 --> 00:33:27.213
We'll lose radio contact shortly.


00:34:31.740 --> 00:34:36.565
3 minutes to analysis completion.


00:34:36.704 --> 00:34:38.567
Receiving beacon transmission.


00:34:42.586 --> 00:34:45.034
Please guys, just 3 minutes...


00:34:45.213 --> 00:34:49.953
Analysis is in progress...


00:34:52.593 --> 00:34:53.882
1 minute passed.


00:35:02.100 --> 00:35:03.679
2 minutes, 30 seconds passed.


00:35:10.818 --> 00:35:12.602
10 seconds to completion.


00:35:13.197 --> 00:35:16.364
9,8,7...


00:35:17.410 --> 00:35:18.491
What is it?


00:35:18.910 --> 00:35:20.489
Signal's lost, sir.


00:35:20.748 --> 00:35:23.368
-Find out why.
-Analysis not possible.


00:35:23.505 --> 00:35:24.869
Scan again.


00:35:32.555 --> 00:35:37.587
System alert...


00:35:38.854 --> 00:35:46.978
System alert...


00:36:00.954 --> 00:36:02.280
Vexille, this way.


00:36:33.111 --> 00:36:34.310
Zak!


00:37:09.234 --> 00:37:11.350
In an entire decade,


00:37:12.069 --> 00:37:16.145
you are our first foreign guests.


00:37:17.863 --> 00:37:20.568
We've quite a welcome for you.


00:37:24.585 --> 00:37:26.967
On my signal, rush for the water.


00:37:27.749 --> 00:37:29.198
I won't go by myself.


00:37:29.319 --> 00:37:32.414
You're the only one with a back-up
transmitter.


00:37:35.340 --> 00:37:36.747
We'll join you later.


00:38:43.994 --> 00:38:45.107
Leon...


00:38:57.882 --> 00:38:59.494
Don't worry, Miss.


00:39:01.015 --> 00:39:03.461
I'm alone. Nothing to be afraid of.


00:39:07.179 --> 00:39:10.388
Maria changed your clothes, not me.


00:39:11.231 --> 00:39:12.384
Maria?


00:39:16.940 --> 00:39:18.225
Don't go outside!


00:39:49.557 --> 00:39:50.615
Leon...


00:40:15.540 --> 00:40:18.036
Do exactly as I say.


00:40:27.011 --> 00:40:28.001
Maria...


00:40:30.935 --> 00:40:34.972
Don't you dare go out again
They're still looking for you.


00:40:35.146 --> 00:40:38.224
Sorry, Maria. It was my fault.


00:40:42.283 --> 00:40:44.521
I never thought SWORD would turn up.


00:40:50.911 --> 00:40:52.320
So much food...


00:40:55.462 --> 00:40:56.738
What about my colleagues?


00:40:59.043 --> 00:41:01.454
-Go cool this.
-Sure.


00:41:02.428 --> 00:41:03.917
What about Leon and the others?


00:41:07.093 --> 00:41:08.965
What happened to Leon Fayden?


00:41:10.974 --> 00:41:13.132
His whereabouts unknown.


00:41:19.232 --> 00:41:20.637
We're still looking.


00:41:39.003 --> 00:41:40.573
This is real.


00:41:41.389 --> 00:41:43.417
It's really rare, y'know...


00:42:06.030 --> 00:42:07.645
You slept for 2 days.


00:42:08.990 --> 00:42:10.477
Get some food in you.


00:42:18.875 --> 00:42:22.872
It was you who sent the messenger
to America?


00:42:32.347 --> 00:42:33.710
One more question.


00:42:34.805 --> 00:42:36.046
Where are we?


00:42:39.941 --> 00:42:43.976
Thie used to be known as Tokyo.


00:42:48.613 --> 00:42:49.977
Tokyo...


00:43:03.296 --> 00:43:06.417
Captain, a second transmission.


00:43:07.630 --> 00:43:08.627
Are you certain?


00:43:08.753 --> 00:43:11.206
Certain, sir.
From the back-up transmitter.


00:43:11.346 --> 00:43:12.878
It's still coming in.


00:43:14.637 --> 00:43:16.676
We're counting on you this time...


00:43:25.483 --> 00:43:27.979
Never used chopsticks before, Miss?


00:43:33.737 --> 00:43:34.819
Tasty?


00:43:50.256 --> 00:43:51.746
That's like magic.


00:43:51.922 --> 00:43:54.083
Where did you hide it?


00:44:05.607 --> 00:44:07.518
Saito's heading this way.


00:44:31.798 --> 00:44:34.163
Most impressive...


00:44:42.396 --> 00:44:47.718
On second thoughts, not.
5 guys for 1 girl?


00:44:48.521 --> 00:44:50.020
That's kinda pathetic.


00:44:52.608 --> 00:44:54.810
Where's the SWORD women?


00:45:02.287 --> 00:45:03.695
Any chick would run


00:45:03.873 --> 00:45:05.362
from a tacky tie like that.


00:45:06.588 --> 00:45:09.080
The boss goes soft on you


00:45:12.382 --> 00:45:13.915
but I don't have his problem.


00:45:15.588 --> 00:45:17.957
I don't know what you're planning


00:45:18.553 --> 00:45:22.216
but whatever you do
it's just a matter of time.


00:45:38.619 --> 00:45:40.357
I'll see you at headquarters.


00:45:46.916 --> 00:45:48.118
He's right.


00:45:51.127 --> 00:45:52.624
It's just a matter of time.


00:46:23.956 --> 00:46:26.448
Daiwa's serious about finding you.


00:46:33.959 --> 00:46:35.287
What is it?


00:46:38.594 --> 00:46:40.415
This place is so full of life.


00:46:48.019 --> 00:46:50.138
I've never seen anywhere like it.


00:46:54.283 --> 00:46:57.145
It makes me nostalgic somehow...


00:47:55.749 --> 00:47:56.869
Bad news.


00:48:50.852 --> 00:48:53.009
Come here...


00:48:54.478 --> 00:48:55.556
Get in there.


00:49:04.109 --> 00:49:06.518
Analysis completion...


00:49:06.660 --> 00:49:09.232
Captain, 3 minutes completed.


00:49:09.447 --> 00:49:11.943
Okay, let's run the analysis.


00:49:15.420 --> 00:49:20.281
Run the feeds from satellites
JC17 & JD15.


00:49:22.133 --> 00:49:24.312
Running analysis.


00:49:26.014 --> 00:49:31.127
Analysis is in progress.


00:49:45.238 --> 00:49:46.642
Nothing there...


00:49:48.158 --> 00:49:51.028
No mountains...no rivers...


00:49:52.707 --> 00:49:53.982
No human habitation...


00:49:55.829 --> 00:49:59.195
What's going on in Tokyo?
Get it up there.


00:50:10.385 --> 00:50:12.793
That's all that's left of Tokyo?


00:50:20.776 --> 00:50:22.677
Daiwa Heavy Industries...


00:50:23.487 --> 00:50:25.350
We've got


00:50:25.485 --> 00:50:27.896
Lt. Commander Vexille Serra's
bio-signature in Tokyo.


00:50:28.073 --> 00:50:30.118
Satellite JD14
is scanning for her now.


00:50:34.074 --> 00:50:35.237
Any other survivors?


00:50:35.370 --> 00:50:36.943
None confirmed.


00:50:37.374 --> 00:50:39.030
Captain, look at this.


00:50:39.162 --> 00:50:40.738
Put it up on screen.


00:50:41.292 --> 00:50:42.909
The red dor is her.


00:50:43.215 --> 00:50:44.452
She's being pursued?


00:50:44.835 --> 00:50:47.002
JD14 is tracking her.


00:50:47.508 --> 00:50:48.878
-Captain?
-What is it?


00:50:49.260 --> 00:50:53.752
The bio-signature map...
it's unfiltered, sir.


00:50:56.144 --> 00:50:59.555
Her bio-signature
is the only one down there.


00:51:01.233 --> 00:51:02.637
How can that be?


00:51:08.818 --> 00:51:10.606
They aren't human?


00:51:12.616 --> 00:51:14.901
Scan the entire country!


00:51:33.425 --> 00:51:34.543
Maria.


00:52:11.052 --> 00:52:12.251
What's this?


00:52:23.432 --> 00:52:26.891
Let's wait to see
if we're being followed.


00:53:03.056 --> 00:53:05.971
They say everything
outside the city's a wasteland.


00:53:06.234 --> 00:53:10.352
Daiwa escaped
to their island fortress.


00:53:11.231 --> 00:53:12.349
Come here.


00:53:13.365 --> 00:53:15.894
That's Daiwa out to sea.


00:53:23.619 --> 00:53:27.368
It's their fault no people are left.


00:53:28.878 --> 00:53:31.912
The Japanese race is extinct.


00:53:33.176 --> 00:53:34.378
But you guys...


00:53:35.843 --> 00:53:38.752
We're not human any more.


00:53:39.767 --> 00:53:41.376
Not human...


00:53:42.890 --> 00:53:46.214
Just fragments of humanity.


00:53:52.899 --> 00:53:54.140
Fragments?


00:53:55.277 --> 00:53:59.066
Fragments that will soon be gone.


00:54:01.080 --> 00:54:05.529
You saw it, right? The final step
between man and machine.


00:54:15.470 --> 00:54:20.293
No red blood left in our veins.


00:54:33.487 --> 00:54:36.431
You're saying none of these people
are human?


00:54:38.617 --> 00:54:39.897
But I'd never seen


00:54:40.032 --> 00:54:41.441
anywhere so alive.


00:54:43.908 --> 00:54:44.943
Trying to hold on


00:54:45.126 --> 00:54:46.800
to their humanity.


00:54:48.625 --> 00:54:51.642
Like eating food
although we don't need to.


00:54:58.093 --> 00:55:02.459
10 years ago, just before
the whole isolation policy


00:55:03.725 --> 00:55:08.676
an unknown disease spread out
from Tokyo.


00:55:11.562 --> 00:55:13.722
Infection brought a raging fever


00:55:14.152 --> 00:55:16.439
with a high mortality rate.


00:55:17.357 --> 00:55:21.646
There was no information about
cause or transmission...


00:55:22.367 --> 00:55:26.149
just a mandatory
immunization program.


00:55:28.944 --> 00:55:32.454
That was the beginning
of our tragedy.


00:55:36.919 --> 00:55:39.079
The disease
was a goverment creation.


00:55:39.762 --> 00:55:42.214
And the vaccination we all received


00:55:42.678 --> 00:55:46.004
was a Daiwa cyber-virus.


00:55:51.734 --> 00:55:54.470
It invades every cell of the body


00:55:54.774 --> 00:55:57.563
converting its molecular structure
into bio-metal


00:55:57.856 --> 00:56:01.232
so that the human body
is replaced by machine from within.


00:56:03.029 --> 00:56:08.858
What was worse, the virus
was still under development.


00:56:09.708 --> 00:56:10.902
Meaning what?


00:56:12.496 --> 00:56:15.623
We were a nation of guinea pigs.


00:56:16.132 --> 00:56:19.288
Japan was their laboratory.


00:56:22.590 --> 00:56:25.377
Finally the brain is owerwritten


00:56:25.934 --> 00:56:31.010
the person becomes an android
and falls under Daiwa's control.


00:56:33.647 --> 00:56:36.351
The speed of the process
differs between people.


00:56:37.189 --> 00:56:42.148
Some of us still cling
to our human consciousness...


00:56:44.782 --> 00:56:47.737
to the fragments of our humanity.


00:56:51.411 --> 00:56:53.240
The technology is half-baked,


00:56:53.963 --> 00:56:57.034
so most turn into junk.


00:56:57.902 --> 00:56:59.291
At best


00:56:59.757 --> 00:57:02.378
we become lumps of metal
with no memory.


00:57:02.802 --> 00:57:04.121
In either case,


00:57:04.761 --> 00:57:09.421
we're miserable specimens
awaiting death.


00:57:12.937 --> 00:57:14.427
How long do you have?


00:57:17.228 --> 00:57:19.180
Daiwa's not done.


00:57:19.486 --> 00:57:23.105
The next target is America.


00:57:26.072 --> 00:57:29.111
They've alredy planted
androids there.


00:57:32.450 --> 00:57:33.652
That politician...


00:57:38.250 --> 00:57:39.823
My buddy, Saga!


00:58:33.602 --> 00:58:34.712
Let;s go!


00:58:53.789 --> 00:58:55.315
We call those, "Jags". Failed


00:58:55.576 --> 00:58:58.401
experiments
from the android process.


00:58:59.046 --> 00:59:03.700
They search around for any kind of
metal absorb it and grow.


00:59:09.549 --> 00:59:11.589
The wasteland's crawling with them.


00:59:13.428 --> 00:59:16.505
They throw up some neat stuff
sometimes, though.


01:00:13.739 --> 01:00:15.106
We should get going.


01:00:18.787 --> 01:00:21.156
Our base is underground.


01:00:39.854 --> 01:00:42.512
Saito, what about that SWORD woman?


01:00:46.234 --> 01:00:47.683
We lost her.


01:00:48.482 --> 01:00:50.057
Failure's dogging you


01:00:50.191 --> 01:00:51.771
since you let that informant
escape to America.


01:00:53.159 --> 01:00:55.480
Maria is harboring the girl.


01:01:01.373 --> 01:01:02.617
Leave them alone.


01:01:04.502 --> 01:01:08.323
SWORD may have penetrated
the R.A.C.E. net.


01:01:08.710 --> 01:01:12.332
Even so, America won't do a thing.


01:01:16.175 --> 01:01:18.004
Relax, Saito.


01:01:18.554 --> 01:01:20.672
Our decade-long experiment


01:01:20.849 --> 01:01:22.345
nears fruition, at last.


01:01:23.139 --> 01:01:27.845
That group, G32 Beta, in the slums


01:01:28.190 --> 01:01:30.643
they alone are perfect specimens.


01:01:34.567 --> 01:01:37.774
Maria is a part of that group.


01:01:38.121 --> 01:01:40.855
Left alone they'll join us
in good time.


01:01:40.995 --> 01:01:42.157
But, sir...


01:01:43.331 --> 01:01:47.364
We need not fear any act of man.


01:02:00.890 --> 01:02:04.842
Very well. Summon Itakura,
Chairman of the slum.


01:02:28.293 --> 01:02:29.155
Hello.


01:02:33.046 --> 01:02:33.917
Here.


01:02:34.716 --> 01:02:36.540
A fresh piece of junk.


01:02:36.844 --> 01:02:39.373
It should contain the part you need.


01:02:39.512 --> 01:02:42.924
Thanks, it's just in time.


01:02:43.437 --> 01:02:44.634
Where's Maria?


01:02:47.188 --> 01:02:50.929
Everyone,
this is Vexille from SWORD.


01:03:10.671 --> 01:03:12.245
Taro, is it ready?


01:03:12.837 --> 01:03:14.115
Darn right it is.


01:03:21.469 --> 01:03:22.670
My suit...


01:03:23.263 --> 01:03:27.179
I fixed it up and
it's ready for action.


01:03:33.527 --> 01:03:34.969
Looking for this?


01:03:40.026 --> 01:03:42.041
-I sent out a beacon signal.
-For how long?


01:03:42.201 --> 01:03:43.317
Longer than 3 minutes.


01:03:43.490 --> 01:03:45.072
The R.A.C.E. net's down?


01:03:45.749 --> 01:03:48.492
Daiwa already reconfigured
the diffusion pattern.


01:03:48.660 --> 01:03:49.610
Darn.


01:03:50.001 --> 01:03:55.412
SWORD
only needs a few minutes to act.


01:03:57.216 --> 01:04:01.081
Another thing, there's one more
SWORD agent at Daiwa HQ.


01:04:02.093 --> 01:04:03.130
Leon?


01:04:03.349 --> 01:04:05.334
Yes, Leon Fayden, I believe.


01:04:11.022 --> 01:04:13.052
Where exactly is he? Any injuries?


01:04:13.186 --> 01:04:15.352
Sorry, that's all I know.


01:04:15.524 --> 01:04:17.012
Taro, what's your source?


01:04:17.171 --> 01:04:20.147
Daiwa's main stream. It's reliable.


01:04:21.277 --> 01:04:22.693
Just Leon, no-one else?


01:04:35.674 --> 01:04:39.500
No luck. No bio-sigmature
readings anywhere.


01:04:41.554 --> 01:04:44.548
I found an additional signature.


01:04:45.842 --> 01:04:48.002
There's just one other.


01:04:54.145 --> 01:04:55.174
What's wrong?


01:04:55.566 --> 01:04:57.970
The electro-magnetic diffusion
has changed.


01:04:58.362 --> 01:04:59.312
Darn.


01:04:59.444 --> 01:05:00.728
I'll re-run the analysis.


01:05:11.082 --> 01:05:14.869
Have Minerva ready to rescue them.


01:05:17.420 --> 01:05:21.371
Captain Borg, a call on the hotline.


01:05:22.758 --> 01:05:25.958
The Defense Secretary alredy?


01:05:26.968 --> 01:05:30.044
No...it's the President.


01:05:42.695 --> 01:05:44.015
Borg, here.


01:05:44.650 --> 01:05:49.942
Yes, Mr. President. That's correct.
7 agents.


01:05:53.248 --> 01:05:57.409
I understand, sir.


01:06:11.224 --> 01:06:15.129
We must abort the mission.


01:06:52.428 --> 01:06:55.175
Takashi, what on earth's going on?


01:06:55.305 --> 01:06:56.963
There's going to be an earthquake.


01:06:57.103 --> 01:06:58.177
There is?


01:06:58.349 --> 01:07:01.342
Yes, it's our last chance.


01:07:02.606 --> 01:07:04.520
We're going to smash Daiwa.


01:07:05.198 --> 01:07:07.064
Me, Maria and the guys...


01:07:10.319 --> 01:07:15.235
3 freight tunnels connect Daiwa
with the mainland.


01:07:17.959 --> 01:07:20.365
Only the main one links to the city.


01:07:20.538 --> 01:07:22.865
The others conect to the wasteland.


01:07:23.001 --> 01:07:24.493
They're all ceramic?


01:07:24.673 --> 01:07:29.999
Yes. A mid-size 'quake is forecast
for the next 24 hours.


01:07:30.132 --> 01:07:32.918
All communication gates are open.
In case of the quake.


01:07:34.181 --> 01:07:35.090
All communication gates are open?


01:07:35.224 --> 01:07:38.091
Correct. And we found a weak point.


01:07:39.390 --> 01:07:41.426
During the earthquake stand-by,


01:07:41.559 --> 01:07:45.809
all tunnel gates
go to auxiliary power


01:07:46.983 --> 01:07:50.522
which creates a 50% delay between
detection of an intruder


01:07:50.702 --> 01:07:54.151
and the gates sealing in response.


01:07:54.655 --> 01:07:57.362
How soon
do they close after detection?


01:07:57.476 --> 01:07:59.234
-18 seconds.
-How far between the gates?


01:07:59.413 --> 01:08:00.741
2,500 meters.


01:08:00.921 --> 01:08:03.367
That's pushing it
even in a fighter suit.


01:08:03.542 --> 01:08:05.538
With our air-buggies, too.


01:08:05.672 --> 01:08:07.159
But it's that or nothing.


01:08:08.086 --> 01:08:09.790
And after you break in?


01:08:14.013 --> 01:08:17.171
We drag this cable behind us.


01:08:21.891 --> 01:08:22.887
The Jags.


01:08:28.402 --> 01:08:30.892
They finish the job
if we get the cable inside.


01:08:31.157 --> 01:08:36.396
This is enough metal to lure them
into the heart of Daiwa.


01:08:37.242 --> 01:08:40.949
Chairman Itakura's called
an emergency council session.


01:08:55.971 --> 01:08:58.676
-Is that all?
-Yes, it is.


01:09:00.269 --> 01:09:02.422
Don't make me repeat myself.


01:09:03.315 --> 01:09:05.388
We don't wish to obstruct


01:09:05.519 --> 01:09:07.304
those who calmly
wait for the end.


01:09:10.072 --> 01:09:12.808
But surely you know Daiwa


01:09:13.196 --> 01:09:15.023
is planning to take America next?


01:09:19.039 --> 01:09:22.822
There's so little time. Excuse me.


01:09:26.497 --> 01:09:28.242
You're determined to go?


01:09:33.136 --> 01:09:38.132
Suppose Daiwa responds
by opening the protective gates?


01:09:40.057 --> 01:09:42.470
This is their precious laboratory.


01:09:43.684 --> 01:09:45.590
They'd never do that.


01:09:51.612 --> 01:09:55.352
In the end
we're all in the same boat...


01:09:55.785 --> 01:09:58.277
trying to protect the same thing.


01:10:02.374 --> 01:10:04.447
It's just that we choose to fight...


01:10:04.580 --> 01:10:07.073
until the very moment
we become scrap metal.


01:10:21.762 --> 01:10:24.802
As an outsider,
it's not my place to speak but...


01:10:26.476 --> 01:10:32.519
your city seems to celebrate
the splendor of what you've lost.


01:10:37.693 --> 01:10:38.941
But Maria...


01:10:40.408 --> 01:10:42.146
she fights for


01:10:42.290 --> 01:10:44.316
the sake of what's not yet gone.


01:11:47.975 --> 01:11:49.922
Foreigners are to be expelled?


01:11:50.730 --> 01:11:52.176
What on earth for?


01:11:55.899 --> 01:11:57.054
Leon...


01:12:20.554 --> 01:12:23.298
Maria, come to America with me.


01:12:27.561 --> 01:12:28.711
What do you mean?


01:12:29.521 --> 01:12:31.677
Your departure permit is invalid.


01:12:31.809 --> 01:12:35.013
Lt. Commander L. Fayden
requested a pass for me.


01:12:35.190 --> 01:12:37.520
No such request was filed.


01:12:37.648 --> 01:12:40.139
That can't be right.
Check once more.


01:12:40.276 --> 01:12:43.898
It comes up negative.
Come with us for questioning.


01:12:44.867 --> 01:12:45.693
Get out.


01:12:45.827 --> 01:12:48.524
What for? Let me call him.


01:12:48.659 --> 01:12:50.571
Calls to the airport are forbidden.


01:12:54.371 --> 01:12:55.703
I'm going with you.


01:12:57.793 --> 01:12:59.577
Let me join your mission.


01:13:01.170 --> 01:13:02.793
It's a Japanese domestic matter.


01:13:02.930 --> 01:13:04.880
Surely it's gone beyond that?


01:13:06.433 --> 01:13:08.838
You're a foreign guest; behave.


01:13:09.893 --> 01:13:11.720
Americans never learn...


01:13:13.395 --> 01:13:16.514
Leon chose to return here
because of you.


01:13:24.654 --> 01:13:28.320
Maria, please take me into Daiwa.


01:13:33.746 --> 01:13:36.197
Keep personal matters out of this.


01:13:39.124 --> 01:13:41.371
I know you want to help Leon, too.


01:13:57.315 --> 01:14:00.179
Takashi, what's wrong?


01:14:01.064 --> 01:14:04.056
Takashi, hold on.


01:14:05.279 --> 01:14:06.565
Takashi!


01:14:08.615 --> 01:14:09.896
Takashi!


01:14:13.293 --> 01:14:14.609
Takashi!


01:14:49.989 --> 01:14:51.228
Takashi!


01:14:55.332 --> 01:14:56.946
Takashi!


01:15:00.587 --> 01:15:02.701
Call yourself human?


01:15:31.035 --> 01:15:33.695
This is our rule.


01:15:34.950 --> 01:15:41.076
Otherwise our plan would be leaked
to Daiwa.


01:17:06.373 --> 01:17:07.620
Vexille.


01:17:10.089 --> 01:17:12.082
We need someone to replace Takashi.


01:17:28.650 --> 01:17:31.765
Once in the tunnel, floor it
or you won't have a chance.


01:17:32.651 --> 01:17:36.316
Take a mid-line to reduce distance.


01:17:37.326 --> 01:17:40.281
Touch the brakes and it's all over.


01:17:42.794 --> 01:17:46.200
I'll lead Team Red
to the East tunnel.


01:17:46.752 --> 01:17:50.914
Saga takes Team Black to the West.


01:17:53.763 --> 01:17:56.713
We've never fielded this many units


01:17:57.473 --> 01:18:00.154
so we don't know how many Jags
will turn up.


01:18:00.727 --> 01:18:04.339
Even if you're the only one left,
don't give up.


01:18:05.437 --> 01:18:08.759
We just need one cable
to reach Daiwa.


01:18:11.735 --> 01:18:15.100
Though we are no more
than fragments...


01:18:15.362 --> 01:18:17.146
we are still human.


01:18:19.288 --> 01:18:24.527
As long as we have our pride
we can still take back our country!


01:19:37.656 --> 01:19:38.478
Maria,


01:19:38.658 --> 01:19:40.350
more Jags than we thought, huh?


01:19:41.116 --> 01:19:42.278
Murata.


01:19:43.159 --> 01:19:45.523
I'll double back and
get them off your tail.


01:20:07.388 --> 01:20:08.670
Team Black to Red.


01:20:08.848 --> 01:20:09.970
Red here.


01:20:15.946 --> 01:20:18.146
Almost to the target gate.


01:20:19.095 --> 01:20:20.140
Roger.


01:20:20.317 --> 01:20:21.603
They're after you!


01:20:35.879 --> 01:20:38.334
Murata!


01:21:01.903 --> 01:21:03.521
We're through the gate.


01:21:22.838 --> 01:21:24.123
Leave it to me.


01:21:50.868 --> 01:21:52.358
2nd gate cleared!


01:22:32.658 --> 01:22:36.077
3rd gate cleared
but we lost Masato's team.


01:22:47.093 --> 01:22:49.711
Maria, we lured them away
from the gate.


01:22:49.847 --> 01:22:51.756
Make another approach.


01:22:52.726 --> 01:22:53.794
Roger.


01:23:06.736 --> 01:23:10.653
The Jags are on the cable already.
They're too fast!


01:23:43.565 --> 01:23:44.723
Maria!


01:24:16.020 --> 01:24:17.003
Vexille.


01:25:29.918 --> 01:25:31.122
One left.


01:25:43.062 --> 01:25:44.095
Maria.


01:27:13.274 --> 01:27:14.641
How come...


01:27:24.449 --> 01:27:25.651
Bravo.


01:27:28.627 --> 01:27:32.747
I guess you didn't expect the tunnel
to be separated from the island?


01:27:36.045 --> 01:27:37.538
What a same.


01:27:38.089 --> 01:27:40.792
Jags can't jump that far.


01:27:44.386 --> 01:27:47.261
Chairman Itakura
kept us well-informed.


01:28:49.041 --> 01:28:50.196
Leon!


01:28:52.041 --> 01:28:54.654
Nice to see you again, Maria.


01:29:01.796 --> 01:29:04.336
We're friends from our student days.


01:29:07.847 --> 01:29:10.135
The 10 years haven't changed you.


01:29:11.182 --> 01:29:16.597
As beautiful
and as dangerous as ever.


01:29:17.570 --> 01:29:19.224
Mr. Kisaragi...


01:29:25.578 --> 01:29:28.653
Nobody move. You're in breach of
international law.


01:29:28.787 --> 01:29:31.194
Nobody move...


01:29:36.293 --> 01:29:37.492
Maria...


01:29:37.961 --> 01:29:39.826
I warned you in vain.


01:29:52.682 --> 01:29:54.426
The irony of fate.


01:29:54.979 --> 01:29:57.717
Hardly imagined I'd see you again.


01:30:00.731 --> 01:30:02.313
I can't let you do that!


01:30:19.418 --> 01:30:20.907
"Insufficent evidence"?


01:30:22.467 --> 01:30:26.918
We're public servants with no chance
against the might of Daiwa.


01:30:28.516 --> 01:30:30.754
It's not just breach of a treaty;


01:30:30.888 --> 01:30:33.302
their research
is a threat to mankind.


01:30:34.809 --> 01:30:36.591
They were released this morning.


01:30:45.736 --> 01:30:48.944
We are the peak of human evolution.


01:30:49.577 --> 01:30:51.068
In fact human existence is nothing.


01:30:51.495 --> 01:30:55.946
But a preparatory stage
in our creation.


01:30:56.624 --> 01:30:59.159
There's nothing evolved about you.


01:31:11.678 --> 01:31:15.800
This body, born of humankind
is perfection.


01:31:16.806 --> 01:31:20.300
Matchless in level of intellect
and stability of emotion.


01:31:21.360 --> 01:31:24.724
No need for sleep nor food.


01:31:25.194 --> 01:31:29.066
Above all, we shall attain
immortality at last.


01:31:31.575 --> 01:31:34.067
What more could be asked?


01:31:37.291 --> 01:31:40.865
You will join me in immortality
soon enough.


01:31:45.173 --> 01:31:48.003
Only the few
will attain this evolution


01:31:48.257 --> 01:31:52.545
and be reborn as Japanese...
the world's strongest race.


01:31:54.639 --> 01:31:57.344
I have done the work of god.


01:31:58.433 --> 01:32:01.302
Maybe I was god all along.


01:32:07.490 --> 01:32:08.727
He's insane.


01:32:17.042 --> 01:32:19.489
But on the eve of completion,


01:32:19.668 --> 01:32:22.950
Japan is empty of
workable specimens.


01:32:24.750 --> 01:32:28.206
But your country abounds in them.


01:32:28.553 --> 01:32:32.293
Healthy subjects
like your dear Leon.


01:33:05.289 --> 01:33:07.281
Nothing divine about you...


01:33:08.132 --> 01:33:10.126
Just another flawed human.


01:33:18.264 --> 01:33:22.762
I had to protect myself for
your sakes against everything.


01:33:23.019 --> 01:33:29.602
Of course I would have the injection
once the virus was safe.


01:33:29.775 --> 01:33:30.895
Such suffering


01:33:31.032 --> 01:33:32.687
for this sicko...


01:33:32.866 --> 01:33:36.650
My research brought you
all eternal life...


01:33:36.953 --> 01:33:41.158
Androids can't act compulsively.


01:33:41.292 --> 01:33:43.492
It doesn't make sense...


01:33:46.081 --> 01:33:49.950
Halt, Saito. Stop it, please.


01:34:05.603 --> 01:34:08.676
The city gates are opening
onto the slums!


01:34:20.116 --> 01:34:23.275
You have the citizens' full support.


01:34:27.084 --> 01:34:29.788
This is Chairman Itakura.


01:34:32.339 --> 01:34:38.125
The Council and I were misguided
and betrayed you all.


01:34:38.342 --> 01:34:42.966
Now, thanks to your brave resolution


01:34:43.184 --> 01:34:47.049
we can make amends for our mistake.


01:34:54.195 --> 01:34:56.691
Thank you all very much.


01:34:57.276 --> 01:34:58.735
Chairman Itakura...


01:35:35.902 --> 01:35:38.229
Detach the central tunnel
from the island!


01:35:38.361 --> 01:35:41.067
A transporter is en route.


01:35:42.788 --> 01:35:46.068
Do not let it arrive.
Detach the tunnel.


01:35:47.955 --> 01:35:50.033
Don't let it in!


01:36:05.392 --> 01:36:06.586
Darn.


01:36:13.731 --> 01:36:15.386
Piece of junk.


01:36:26.748 --> 01:36:30.111
As long as I have my research


01:36:30.460 --> 01:36:33.698
the world can still be mine.


01:36:43.930 --> 01:36:47.552
The Jags will be here soon.


01:37:38.939 --> 01:37:41.682
I'll get him, you look after Leon.


01:37:41.865 --> 01:37:43.191
No, I'll go after him...


01:37:44.240 --> 01:37:46.066
Not with that leg, you won't.


01:37:49.949 --> 01:37:51.282
Look after Leon for me.


01:40:18.597 --> 01:40:20.007
Maria...


01:40:21.393 --> 01:40:25.638
Why didn't you come to the airport?


01:40:47.045 --> 01:40:49.203
I hate machines


01:40:49.466 --> 01:40:51.706
but humans like you
are far worse.


01:41:00.225 --> 01:41:01.469
Vexille!


01:41:27.836 --> 01:41:29.034
Vexille.


01:41:30.589 --> 01:41:31.753
Where's Maria?


01:41:56.155 --> 01:41:59.650
Stay back, you heap of junk!


01:42:00.289 --> 01:42:01.863
The Jags will get you soon.


01:42:03.328 --> 01:42:04.447
Maria.


01:42:08.716 --> 01:42:10.244
Maria, run!


01:42:11.878 --> 01:42:15.247
Now we'll be together forever.


01:42:46.041 --> 01:42:49.280
Maria!


01:44:57.629 --> 01:45:01.497
Jags across Japan came
to destroy Daiwa


01:45:02.511 --> 01:45:05.333
then sank deep beneath the sea.


01:45:08.846 --> 01:45:11.424
Maria and her kind died off.


01:45:13.234 --> 01:45:19.513
But they left us something vital
we should carry with us.


01:45:21.405 --> 01:45:23.644
It was Maria that taught us


01:45:25.241 --> 01:45:27.861
as long as we communicate hope
to the next generation


01:45:29.206 --> 01:45:33.321
we ourselves gain eternal existence.

